1
00:02:08,530 --> 00:02:10,860
Look at me. Look at me!

2
00:02:11,220 --> 00:02:13,980
Do you remember me now, boy, eh?

3
00:02:13,980 --> 00:02:17,080
Remember me? There's a bright boy.

4
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:20,160
You'll be coming with me, boy,

5
00:02:20,230 --> 00:02:23,450
and you'll be keeping your mouth shut.

6
00:02:39,710 --> 00:02:42,870
- Keep your mouth shut, boy. - I'm not a boy!

7
00:02:42,870 --> 00:02:45,710
You're not a smart boy, is that what you're trying to say?

8
00:02:45,710 --> 00:02:47,490
Do you want to live, boy?!

9
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:54,390
North, boy, we're going north.

10
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:28,460
It had three eyes.

11
00:03:29,170 --> 00:03:31,860
It told me to come with him, so I did.

12
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:35,870
We went down into the crypts and my father was there.

13
00:03:35,870 --> 00:03:38,720
Your father's not down there, little lord.

14
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:40,890
Not for many years yet.

15
00:03:42,350 --> 00:03:45,600
You're afraid... just like Hodor.

16
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,550
I'm not afraid of some hole in the ground.

17
00:03:47,550 --> 00:03:50,640
You've lived beyond the Wall. What are you scared of?

18
00:03:51,350 --> 00:03:53,960
I'm a crippled boy and I'm willing to go.

19
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:02,030
That's my grandfather Lord Rickard.

20
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:05,490
He was burned alive by the Mad King Aerys.

21
00:04:06,630 --> 00:04:09,160
That's Lyanna, my father's sister.

22
00:04:09,410 --> 00:04:11,620
King Robert was supposed to marry her,

23
00:04:11,620 --> 00:04:14,050
but Rhaegar Targaryen kidnapped her.

24
00:04:15,110 --> 00:04:17,410
Robert started a war to win her back.

25
00:04:17,410 --> 00:04:20,730
He killed Rhaegar, but she died anyway.

26
00:04:21,780 --> 00:04:23,690
That's where I saw father.

27
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:28,360
You see? He's not here.

28
00:04:36,950 --> 00:04:40,010
- Here, shaggydog. - Rickon!

29
00:04:40,620 --> 00:04:43,880
That beast is supposed to be chained in the kennels!

30
00:04:43,880 --> 00:04:47,200
- He doesn't like chains. - What are you doing down here?

31
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:50,410
- Come back up with us. - No, I came to see father.

32
00:04:50,410 --> 00:04:53,520
How many times have I told you? He's in King's Landing

33
00:04:53,520 --> 00:04:55,270
with Sansa and Arya.

34
00:04:55,330 --> 00:04:57,810
He was down here. I saw him.

35
00:04:57,810 --> 00:04:59,210
Saw him when?

36
00:04:59,530 --> 00:05:01,190
Last night,

37
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:03,160
when I was sleeping.

38
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:05,740
Here, Shaggydog.

39
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:13,570
You both miss him.

40
00:05:13,750 --> 00:05:16,390
It's only natural he should be in your thoughts

41
00:05:16,390 --> 00:05:20,580
and dreams, but that doesn't mean that...

42
00:05:21,590 --> 00:05:23,020
Bran...

43
00:05:40,970 --> 00:05:42,870
- My lady. - My lady.

44
00:05:42,990 --> 00:05:44,430
- My lady. - My lady.

45
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:47,000
- My lady. - My lady.

46
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:49,490
My lady.

47
00:06:38,550 --> 00:06:39,790
Robb.

48
00:06:41,550 --> 00:06:42,660
Robb.

49
00:06:46,630 --> 00:06:47,820
Robb!

50
00:06:52,470 --> 00:06:54,740
You've ruined your sword.

51
00:07:07,540 --> 00:07:09,670
I'll kill them all...

52
00:07:11,840 --> 00:07:13,340
...every one of them.

53
00:07:14,660 --> 00:07:16,580
I will kill them all.

54
00:07:18,330 --> 00:07:19,640
My boy.

55
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:24,550
They have your sisters.

56
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:28,680
We have to get the girls back.

57
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:33,030
And then we will kill them all.

58
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:43,640
*The boar's great tusks, they boded ill*

59
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:47,410
*for good King Robert's health*

60
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:51,630
*and the beast was every bit as fat*

61
00:07:52,070 --> 00:07:54,930
*as Robert was himself*

62
00:07:55,660 --> 00:07:59,710
*But our brave king cried, "Do your worst!*

63
00:07:59,710 --> 00:08:02,280
*I'll have your ugly head!*

64
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:06,660
*You're nowhere near as murd'rous as*

65
00:08:08,220 --> 00:08:10,840
*the lion in my bed"*

66
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:15,580
*King Robert lost his battle and*

67
00:08:16,090 --> 00:08:19,510
*he failed his final test*

68
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:25,280
*The lion ripped his balls off and*

69
00:08:27,450 --> 00:08:29,740
*the boar did all the rest*

70
00:08:43,920 --> 00:08:45,380
Very amusing.

71
00:08:45,850 --> 00:08:47,500
Isn't it a funny song?

72
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:51,060
Thank you for your rendition.

73
00:08:51,340 --> 00:08:54,070
I imagine it was even better received at that tavern.

74
00:08:54,070 --> 00:08:55,870
I'm so sorry, your grace.

75
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:58,620
I'll never sing it again, I swear.

76
00:08:58,630 --> 00:09:00,570
Tell me, which do you favor:

77
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:03,210
your fingers or your tongue?

78
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:05,190
Your grace?

79
00:09:05,210 --> 00:09:06,650
Fingers or your tongue?

80
00:09:06,650 --> 00:09:08,980
If you got to keep one, which would it be?

81
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:13,180
I... I...

82
00:09:13,180 --> 00:09:15,290
Or I could just cut your throat.

83
00:09:16,920 --> 00:09:18,980
Every man needs hands, your grace.

84
00:09:18,980 --> 00:09:20,060
Good.

85
00:09:20,690 --> 00:09:23,290
- Tongue it is. - Your grace, please.

86
00:09:23,570 --> 00:09:25,570
I won't sing... your grace.

87
00:09:25,570 --> 00:09:27,620
Ser Ilyn, who better than you

88
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:29,750
- to carry out the sentence? - I beg you!

89
00:09:29,750 --> 00:09:31,050
Please no.

90
00:09:33,070 --> 00:09:34,110
No!

91
00:09:37,060 --> 00:09:39,830
Your grace, please. I beg you, I will never sing again!

92
00:09:39,830 --> 00:09:42,810
- I'm done for the day. - No-oooo!

93
00:09:42,810 --> 00:09:45,130
I'll leave the rest of the matters to you, mother.

94
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:49,820
Your grace, please!

95
00:09:57,760 --> 00:09:59,050
You look quite nice.

96
00:10:00,190 --> 00:10:01,370
Thank you, my lord.

97
00:10:01,380 --> 00:10:03,780
"Your grace." I'm king now.

98
00:10:04,090 --> 00:10:07,370
Stop-ppp! No!

99
00:10:07,370 --> 00:10:10,090
Walk with me. I want to show you something.

100
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:16,170
Do as you're bid, child.

101
00:10:23,620 --> 00:10:26,350
And as soon as you've had your blood, I'll put a son in you.

102
00:10:26,750 --> 00:10:28,680
Mother says that shouldn't be long.

103
00:10:33,230 --> 00:10:34,920
No, please no!

104
00:10:35,970 --> 00:10:37,660
This one's your father.

105
00:10:38,490 --> 00:10:40,000
This one here.

106
00:10:41,420 --> 00:10:43,910
Look at it and see what happens to traitors.

107
00:10:44,020 --> 00:10:46,770
- You promised to be merciful. - I was.

108
00:10:46,990 --> 00:10:49,060
I gave him a clean death.

109
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:52,160
Look at him.

110
00:10:52,270 --> 00:10:53,810
Please let me go home.

111
00:10:53,810 --> 00:10:55,510
I won't do any treason, I swear.

112
00:10:55,510 --> 00:10:59,040
Mother says I'm still to marry you. So you'll stay here

113
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:00,390
and obey.

114
00:11:02,390 --> 00:11:04,080
Look at him!

115
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:13,850
Well?

116
00:11:14,380 --> 00:11:16,550
How long do I have to look?

117
00:11:18,710 --> 00:11:20,890
As long as it pleases me.

118
00:11:23,580 --> 00:11:25,350
Do you want to see the rest?

119
00:11:25,350 --> 00:11:27,680
If it please your grace.

120
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:30,530
That's your septa there.

121
00:11:31,990 --> 00:11:33,550
I'll tell you what:

122
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:35,470
I'm going to give you a present.

123
00:11:36,030 --> 00:11:37,690
After I raise my armies

124
00:11:37,690 --> 00:11:39,680
and kill your traitor brother,

125
00:11:39,680 --> 00:11:42,550
I'm going to give you his head as well.

126
00:11:42,890 --> 00:11:45,130
Or maybe he'll give me yours.

127
00:11:50,560 --> 00:11:53,750
My mother tells me a king should never strike his lady.

128
00:11:54,630 --> 00:11:56,120
Ser Meryn.

129
00:12:17,730 --> 00:12:19,620
Here, girl.

130
00:12:23,730 --> 00:12:25,350
Will you obey now?

131
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:28,400
Or do you need another lesson?

132
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:33,410
I'll look for you in court.

133
00:12:36,740 --> 00:12:39,100
Save yourself some pain, girl.

134
00:12:39,140 --> 00:12:40,890
Give him what he wants.

135
00:12:42,980 --> 00:12:44,930
You'll be needing that again.

136
00:13:05,730 --> 00:13:07,950
The proper course is clear:

137
00:13:08,060 --> 00:13:10,550
Pledge fealty to King Renly and move south

138
00:13:10,550 --> 00:13:12,660
to join our forces with his.

139
00:13:13,590 --> 00:13:15,740
Renly is not the king.

140
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:18,840
You cannot mean to hold to Joffrey, my lord.

141
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:20,560
He put your father to death.

142
00:13:20,560 --> 00:13:22,660
That doesn't make Renly king.

143
00:13:22,780 --> 00:13:25,260
He's Robert's youngest brother.

144
00:13:26,030 --> 00:13:28,530
If Bran can't be lord of Winterfell before me,

145
00:13:28,540 --> 00:13:30,660
Renly can't be king before Stannis.

146
00:13:30,670 --> 00:13:32,640
Do you mean to declare us for Stannis?

147
00:13:32,640 --> 00:13:35,410
- Renly is not right! - My lords.

148
00:13:35,410 --> 00:13:37,810
- If we put ourselves behind Stannis... - My lords!

149
00:13:38,330 --> 00:13:41,850
Here is what I say to these two kings...

150
00:13:44,420 --> 00:13:47,670
Renly Baratheon is nothing to me,

151
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:49,620
nor Stannis neither.

152
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:52,100
Why should they rule over me and mine

153
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:54,970
from some flowery seat in the south?

154
00:13:54,970 --> 00:13:58,980
What do they know of the Wall or the Wolfswood?

155
00:13:59,580 --> 00:14:02,050
Even their gods are wrong!

156
00:14:05,270 --> 00:14:08,130
Why shouldn't we rule ourselves again?

157
00:14:08,710 --> 00:14:11,410
It was the dragons we bowed to

158
00:14:11,480 --> 00:14:14,480
and now the dragons are dead!

159
00:14:15,540 --> 00:14:18,490
There sits the only king

160
00:14:18,490 --> 00:14:21,360
I mean to bend my knee to...

161
00:14:21,800 --> 00:14:23,910
The King in the North!

162
00:14:31,750 --> 00:14:34,280
I'll have peace on those terms.

163
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:36,560
They can keep their Red Castle

164
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:39,090
and their iron chair too.

165
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:42,420
The King in the North!

166
00:14:44,060 --> 00:14:47,220
Am I your brother, now and always?

167
00:14:47,230 --> 00:14:48,840
Now and always.

168
00:14:52,450 --> 00:14:56,120
My sword is yours, in victory and defeat

169
00:14:56,130 --> 00:14:58,780
from this day until my last day.

170
00:14:59,780 --> 00:15:01,560
The King in the North!

171
00:15:01,570 --> 00:15:05,310
The King in the North! The King in the North!

172
00:15:05,330 --> 00:15:07,290
The King in the North!

173
00:15:07,290 --> 00:15:10,920
The King in the North! The King in the North!

174
00:15:10,920 --> 00:15:12,940
The King in the North!

175
00:15:12,940 --> 00:15:14,730
The King in the North!

176
00:15:14,790 --> 00:15:16,660
The King in the North!

177
00:15:16,670 --> 00:15:18,520
The King in the North!

178
00:15:18,790 --> 00:15:24,880
The King in the North! The King in the North!

179
00:15:28,890 --> 00:15:31,560
- Lady Stark. - I want to see him.

180
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:33,910
Now!

181
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:56,190
Leave us.

182
00:16:02,010 --> 00:16:04,520
You look lovely tonight, Lady Stark.

183
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:06,940
Widowhood becomes you.

184
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:11,380
Your bed must be lonely.

185
00:16:11,590 --> 00:16:13,380
Is that why you came?

186
00:16:14,580 --> 00:16:15,880
I'm not at my best,

187
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:18,320
but I think I could be of service.

188
00:16:18,650 --> 00:16:22,150
You slip out of that gown and we'll see if I'm up to...

189
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:29,690
Oh, I do like a violent woman.

190
00:16:29,690 --> 00:16:33,320
I will kill you tonight, Ser,

191
00:16:33,450 --> 00:16:36,580
pack your head in a box and send it to your sister.

192
00:16:36,580 --> 00:16:38,310
Let me show you how...

193
00:16:38,310 --> 00:16:40,510
Hit me again, over the ear.

194
00:16:40,510 --> 00:16:42,330
And again and again.

195
00:16:43,620 --> 00:16:45,910
You're stronger than you look... it shouldn't take long.

196
00:16:45,910 --> 00:16:47,770
That is what you want the world to believe, isn't it?

197
00:16:47,770 --> 00:16:49,370
That you don't fear death.

198
00:16:49,370 --> 00:16:51,020
But I don't, my lady.

199
00:16:51,750 --> 00:16:55,100
The dark is coming for all of us. Why cry about it?

200
00:16:55,100 --> 00:16:57,240
Because you are going to the deepest

201
00:16:57,240 --> 00:17:00,120
of the seven hells, if the gods are just.

202
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:02,020
What gods are those?

203
00:17:02,970 --> 00:17:05,500
The trees your husband prayed to?

204
00:17:05,980 --> 00:17:09,380
Where were the trees when his head was getting chopped off?

205
00:17:09,690 --> 00:17:12,920
If your gods are real and if they are just,

206
00:17:13,120 --> 00:17:15,770
why is the world so full of injustice?

207
00:17:16,690 --> 00:17:19,640
Because of men like you.

208
00:17:20,670 --> 00:17:24,020
There are no men like me. Only me.

209
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:32,890
My son Bran.

210
00:17:33,930 --> 00:17:36,480
How did he come to fall from that tower?

211
00:17:36,480 --> 00:17:38,110
I pushed him out the window.

212
00:17:41,530 --> 00:17:42,890
Why?

213
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:47,730
I hoped the fall would kill him.

214
00:17:47,730 --> 00:17:48,880
Why?

215
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:59,290
You should get some sleep.

216
00:17:59,470 --> 00:18:01,430
It's going to be a long war.

217
00:18:26,740 --> 00:18:28,860
I can't believe we're actually at war.

218
00:18:30,630 --> 00:18:33,960
Was it this exciting last time, when you were young?

219
00:18:37,220 --> 00:18:38,640
What does it say?

220
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:42,560
Have we captured Robb Stark yet?

221
00:18:43,090 --> 00:18:45,670
- What's our next move? - Stop talking.

222
00:18:46,530 --> 00:18:48,300
Get back into bed.

223
00:18:56,790 --> 00:18:58,610
They have my son.

224
00:19:01,780 --> 00:19:04,520
The Stark boy appears to be less green than we'd hoped.

225
00:19:04,520 --> 00:19:07,770
I've heard his wolf killed a dozen men and as many horses.

226
00:19:07,770 --> 00:19:09,560
Is it true about Stannis and Renly?

227
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:12,340
Both Baratheon brothers have taken up against us.

228
00:19:12,340 --> 00:19:15,020
Jaime captured, his armies scattered...

229
00:19:15,020 --> 00:19:16,660
It's a catastrophe.

230
00:19:17,580 --> 00:19:20,160
Perhaps we should sue for peace.

231
00:19:23,640 --> 00:19:25,450
There's your peace.

232
00:19:26,130 --> 00:19:27,110
Joffrey saw to that

233
00:19:27,310 --> 00:19:29,990
when he decided to remove Ned Stark's head.

234
00:19:30,530 --> 00:19:33,080
You'll have an easier time drinking from that cup

235
00:19:33,080 --> 00:19:35,970
than you will bringing Robb Stark to the table now.

236
00:19:36,240 --> 00:19:37,710
He's winning...

237
00:19:37,710 --> 00:19:39,560
in case you hadn't noticed.

238
00:19:39,570 --> 00:19:41,790
I'm told we still have his sisters.

239
00:19:41,790 --> 00:19:44,280
The first order of business is ransoming Ser Jaime.

240
00:19:44,280 --> 00:19:46,510
No truces. We can't afford to look weak.

241
00:19:46,510 --> 00:19:47,760
We should march on them at once.

242
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:50,110
First we must return to Casterly Rock to raise...

243
00:19:50,110 --> 00:19:52,570
They have my son!

244
00:19:55,470 --> 00:19:57,490
Get out, all of you.

245
00:20:08,180 --> 00:20:09,640
Not you.

246
00:20:25,260 --> 00:20:27,830
You were right about Eddard Stark.

247
00:20:29,750 --> 00:20:31,620
If he were alive, we could have used him

248
00:20:31,620 --> 00:20:34,400
to broker a peace with Winterfell and Riverrun,

249
00:20:35,760 --> 00:20:37,260
which would have given us more time

250
00:20:37,260 --> 00:20:40,320
to deal with Robert's brothers. But now...

251
00:20:41,510 --> 00:20:45,080
madness... madness and stupidity.

252
00:20:47,820 --> 00:20:50,530
I always thought you were a stunted fool.

253
00:20:52,200 --> 00:20:54,130
Perhaps I was wrong.

254
00:20:54,180 --> 00:20:55,700
Half wrong.

255
00:20:57,530 --> 00:20:59,840
I'm new to strategy, but...

256
00:21:00,230 --> 00:21:02,660
unless we want to be surrounded by three armies,

257
00:21:02,660 --> 00:21:04,360
it appears we can't stay here.

258
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:06,230
No one will stay here.

259
00:21:07,130 --> 00:21:09,840
Ser Gregor will head out with 500 riders

260
00:21:09,850 --> 00:21:13,820
and set the Riverland on fire from God's Eye to the Red Fork.

261
00:21:14,330 --> 00:21:17,090
The rest of us will regroup at Harrenhal.

262
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:20,940
And you will go to King's Landing.

263
00:21:22,440 --> 00:21:23,690
And do what?

264
00:21:23,690 --> 00:21:24,940
Rule!

265
00:21:26,010 --> 00:21:29,100
You will serve as Hand of the King in my stead.

266
00:21:29,290 --> 00:21:30,580
You will bring that boy king

267
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:33,070
to heel and his mother too, if needs be.

268
00:21:33,070 --> 00:21:34,150
And if you get so much

269
00:21:34,150 --> 00:21:36,230
as a whiff of treason from any of the rest:

270
00:21:36,230 --> 00:21:37,680
Baelish, Varys, Pycelle...

271
